## Reading the results

- Reachable through the proxy: all 36 sources answered (no connection failures), but status alone is misleading. The first-200-byte excerpts show bot challenges behind four answers: DBLP (202, title "Making sure you're not a bot!"), and npm (403), ACM DL (403) and SSRN (403), each titled "Just a moment...". ScienceDirect (403) and IEEE Xplore (418) are refusals whose first 200 bytes do not show their nature; Semantic Scholar (429) returned a JSON "Too Many Requests" message.
- Check 3.1 did not reach example.com: the 503 is an HTML page titled "The Website is Blocked" that links to `urlfilter.kaust.edu.sa`, i.e. an upstream URL filter, not the world proxy's JSON refusal that the other four checks show.
- Refused by the world proxy: example.org (deny list) and the metadata and `localtest.me` addresses (not public) return 403.
- `forge release download` is unsupported in this world; curl is the working download path.
- Large payloads: a 160 MiB file and 1,500 small files were committed and pushed in one commit.
